Examining the code of the method DoubleMetaphone.doubleMetaphone(String, boolean) shows that the method processes each character in the input string and handles the character 'G' by invoking handleG(...).

Looking into the handleG(...) method reveals that it checks if 'G' is followed by "IER" in this code snippet:
```
else if (contains(value, index + 1, 1, "E", "I", "Y") || 
         contains(value, index - 1, 4, "AGGI", "OGGI")) {
     // Some Germanic checks
     if ((contains(...)) || contains(..., "ET")) {
         result.append('K');
